  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: S Augustodurum</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In the 19th century, A. de Caumont hypothesized an aqueduct to supply Augustodurum from the south (i.e., from the modern communes of Juaye-Mondaye and Monceaux-en-Bessin). This idea was repeated in TIR Condate whence BAtlas, but more recently it has been called into question.",
